      "widgets_values": [
        "# Upgrade — Source Preserve Turbo (tested example)\n\nRTX 3090 / normal ComfyUI port 8188. Press Run on that worker.\nThe Base, Qwen, VAE and sampler nodes enforce this worker server-side. The 4070 and legacy --disable-dynamic-vram workers are rejected before any model-loading branch. Existing production workflows are unchanged.\n\nA FAST SOURCE-PRESERVATION option, not stronger High or an upscaler. The accepted genuine navy-shirt/closet example kept credible likeness/pose with smoother skin than Quality50; it did not recover more factual background detail. A fresh normal-3090 runtime check is tracked separately. Historical 4070 timings are not this worker's benchmark.\n\nBase9B FP8 + QwenFP8mixed + full Flux2 VAE. Turbo1 → Mitch V3 step1600 .90 → Smartphone .25. 8 Euler / CFG1,816×1088, fixed seed8675412. One genuine source bicubic1MP feeds native whole-image VAE reference latents on BOTH branches. Rendering starts from an empty latent; small details are regenerated rather than copied. No masks, swap, restoration, upscaler or second pass.\n\nThe source and prompt are ordinary editable controls, but THIS PROMPT describes the navy sweatshirt, white neckline and closet example. For another genuine photograph, review and rewrite those details and BOTH output-dimension nodes before Run. A changed source/prompt/seed is UNVALIDATED. This is not a universal enhancer or exact gaze/identity lock. Exact default-source SHA256 and source-graph provenance are in config/production-speed-solo-upgrade.json.\n\nReview the entire result against its own source: recognizable face, age, closed lips, gaze, pose, clothing, room geometry and integration. Do not count the source photograph as an independent likeness reference. Run resamples even with a fixed seed. Images save to production-speed/upgrade-source-preserve; SaveImage increments filenames. Historical photos remain untouched.\n"
      ]
    }
